-- title:
--   Multi-radical Kummer extensions are abelian of exponent n
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ and $L$ be fields with $L$ a $K$-algebra, let $n$ be a natural number, and assume the set $\mathrm{primitiveRoots}\ n\ K$ of primitive $n$-th roots of unity in $K$ is nonempty (which forces $n>0$ and $n\neq 0$ in $K$). Let $S$ be a finite set of units of $K$, and assume $L$ is a splitting field over $K$ of the polynomial $\prod_{u\in S}(X^{n}-C(u))$, where each $u\in S$ is viewed in $K$ through the unit map. The conclusion is a threefold conjunction: $L$ is Galois over $K$ in the Mathlib sense (normal and separable as a $K$-algebra); any two $K$-algebra automorphisms $\sigma,\tau$ of $L$ commute, $\sigma\tau=\tau\sigma$; and every $K$-algebra automorphism $\sigma$ of $L$ satisfies $\sigma^{n}=1$. Thus $\mathrm{Gal}(L/K)$ is abelian of exponent dividing $n$. Note that the conclusion is stated for the automorphism group $L\simeq_{\mathrm{alg}[K]}L$ itself, not via a chosen isomorphism with a subgroup of $\mu_n^{|S|}$, and that the case $S=\varnothing$ is permitted.
--
--   This is the elementary half of Kummer theory for several radicals simultaneously: over a field containing $\mu_n$, a compositum of radical extensions $K(u^{1/n})$, $u\in S$, is abelian of exponent dividing $n$. Mathlib covers the single-radical case; this statement is the multi-radical form used in the description of the relevant power subgroup as generated by such splitting fields and, downstream, in the class-field-theoretic norm-index estimates for number fields.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_KummerTheory_isGalois_and_commute_and_pow_eq_one_of_isSplittingField_prod_X_pow_sub_C.lean

